Correct the TSO STEPLIB library allocation to ensure all concatenated libraries are authorized OR invoke EYU9XENF using a TSO batch job as follows:


//EYU9XENF JOB (nnnn),'userid',CLASS=A,REGION=32M,MSGCLASS=A,
// NOTIFY=userid
//EYU9XENF EXEC PGM=IKJEFT01,
// REGION=2M,DYNAMNBR=99
//STEPLIB DD DISP=SHR,DSN=&HLQ..SEYUAUTH
//SYSTSPRT DD SYSOUT=*
//SYSTSIN DD *
EYU9XENF
/*
Replace the userid with your TSO userid, nnnn with job account information and &HLQ with the CPSM high level qualifier of the SEYUAUTH dataset.

*  Sample JCL to run FM/IMS under TSO as a work around:

    //STEP01   EXEC PGM=IKJEFT01,DYNAMNBR=100
    //SYSTSIN  DD *
      CALL 'FMN.SFMNMOD1(FMNIMS)'
    //SYSPRINT DD SYSOUT=*
    //SYSTSPRT DD SYSOUT=*
    //FMIMSIN DD *
    $$FILEM IEB REGNTYPE=DLI,
       .
       .
       .
    $$FILEM     PROC=*
    EXIT
    /*

